f_snaps":59,"epa_per_play":-0.1121,"pass_rate":0.4407,"pass_rate_neutral":0.4211,"def_epa_per_play":-0.08064},{"week":8,"opponent":"JAX","home":false,"pf":7.0,"pa":42.0,"off_snaps":58,"epa_per_play":-0.4853,"pass_rate":0.5862,"pass_rate_neutral":0.6111,"def_epa_per_play":0.1987},{"week":9,"opponent":"DAL","home":true,"pf":23.0,"pa":27.0,"off_snaps":59,"epa_per_play":-0.2082,"pass_rate":0.6102,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5312,"def_epa_per_play":0.1397}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2023,"team":"GB","distance":0.4439,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"},{"season":2023,"team":"CLE","distance":0.54,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Kevin Stefanski"},{"season":2025,"team":"DAL","distance":0.5809,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Brian Schottenheimer"},{"season":2025,"team":"LV","distance":0.5971,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Chip Kelly"},{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.5995,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Matt LaFleur"}],"defense":[{"season":2025,"team":"GB","distance":0.2135,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2022,"team":"NO","distance":0.2597,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennis Allen"},{"season":2025,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3164,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Dennard Wilson"},{"season":2022,"team":"CHI","distance":0.3285,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2023,"team":"CIN","distance":0.3291,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Lou Anarumo"}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Colts are 2-7 through week 9 of the 2026 season and have been outscored 249 to 184. Neither side has held up so far, with the offense 29th in EPA per play and the defense 27th in EPA allowed. Their most distinctive trait is the 2nd lowest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Colts offense has struggled, ranking 25th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their run and pass mix has stayed close to what game situations call for. Daniel Jones has run the passing game, with Keenan Allen leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Colts have one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 27th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Even its strongest area, success rate allowed, only ranks 14th, and it is 32nd in EPA allowed per rush. Laiatu Latu has been as productive as expected, but the bigger surprise is Adetomiwa Adebawore, who has 4 sacks despite playing only 46% of the snaps. In terms of scheme, they have the 2nd lowest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Colts have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 92% of field goals, which is well above average. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into the secondary, about 29% of the money on the books. Their tight ends were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Daniel Jones has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,722 yards. Targets have been spread around, with Keenan Allen and Josh Downs leading a group where nobody has more than a fifth of the looks. Jonathan Taylor has handled most of the work in the backfield with 74% of the carries. On defense, DeForest Buckner leads the team with 4 sacks.","coaching":"Shane Steichen is calling the offense as head coach and Lou Anarumo is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Packers under Matt LaFleur and the 2023 Browns under Kevin Stefanski. Their defense looks most like the 2025 Packers and the 2022 Saints under Dennis Allen.","trends":"The offense went from 9th in EPA per play in 2025 to 29th so far this season, a big step back. The defense moved from 16th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 27th so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was two point attempt rate, which went from 13% to 0%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}